  "emailBody": "\n        <html>\n\n        <body\n            style=\"\n                font-family:Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif;\n                margin:20px;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    background:#d42e12;\n                    color:white;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                \"\n            >\n\n\n               <h1 style=\"margin:0;\">\n                    Fuel Market Intelligence Evening Report\n                </h1>\n\n                <p style=\"margin:5px 0 0 0;\">\n                    11 August 2026\n                </p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <p\n                style=\"\n                    font-size:16px;\n                    margin-top:20px;\n                    margin-bottom:20px;\n                \"\n            >\n                Good evening Sir,\n                <br><br>\n                \n                Here is today's fuel market intelligence report highlighting\n                the latest PMS and AGO depot prices together with key industry\n                developments and market news.\n            </p>\n\n            <br>\n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            PMS Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average PMS Prices: ₦1,206.00/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>INTERGRATED</td>\n                <td>₦1,200.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,200.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,200.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MASTERS</td>\n                <td>₦1,217.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>BULK STRATEGIC</td>\n                <td>₦1,217.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>LIQUID BULK</td>\n                <td>₦1,217.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SIGMUND</td>\n                <td>₦1,217.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,180.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            AGO Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average AGO Prices: ₦1,726.88/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>WOSBAB</td>\n                <td>₦1,785.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,740.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,700.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,750.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>ZAMSON</td>\n                <td>₦1,800.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>ARDOVA</td>\n                <td>₦1,750.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>ARADEL</td>\n                <td>₦1,540.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,750.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Fuel Price Hike Imminent as Brent Hits $90\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Lagos diesel prices already moving higher on Tuesday following a cautious trading session the previous day. The latest movement followed a sharp recovery in crude prices as expectations of an early reopening of the Strait of Hormuz weakened. Individual depot prices remain dependent on supply positions and procurement costs.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/fuel-price-hike-imminent-as-brent-hits-90\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    NMDPRA Moves to Resolve Crude Supply Shortages to Local Refineries\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria is working with the Nigerian Upstream Petroleum Regulatory Commission (NUPRC) to resolve crude oil supply shortages to local refineries. NMDPRA Chief Executive Rabiu Umar disclosed this at the 49th Nigeria Annual International Conference and Exhibition.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nmdpra-moves-to-resolve-crude-supply-shortages-to-local-refineries\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Refineries Were Shut Down Over Losses, Not Failure to Produce – PENGASSAN\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria’s state-owned refineries were shut down because their operations were commercially unviable, the outgoing President of the Petroleum and Natural Gas Senior Staff Association of Nigeria said. Festus Osifo said the Nigerian National Petroleum Company Limited was forced to halt operations after it became clear that the cost of processing crude exceeded the value of the petroleum products generated from the refineries.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/refineries-were-shut-down-over-losses-not-failure-to-produce-pengassan\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Strait of Hormuz Traffic Worsens as Brent Crude Nears $90\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude was trading at $88.04 per barrel, up 0.36%. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) stood at $82.50, gaining 0.45 per cent. Murban crude was quoted at $84.90, up 5.79 per cent, while natural gas declined 0.64 per cent to $2.776.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/strait-of-hormuz-traffic-worsens-as-brent-crude-nears-90\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Depot Diesel Prices Jump as Marketers Anticipate Crude Oil Surge Amid Hormuz Uncertainty\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria’s diesel market turned sharply bullish on Monday as depot owners raised Automotive Gas Oil (AGO) prices. The sharp intra-day adjustments came as marketers reassessed the market following the rise in crude oil prices. A number of depots reportedly stopped selling during the day rather than commit available volumes at their earlier prices.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/depot-diesel-prices-jump-as-marketers-anticipate-crude-oil-surge-amid-hormuz-uncertainty\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
